- `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml compile exec:java -Dexec.args='acl-fixture /Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic/fixtures/security/acl-signatures.json'` — passed; fixture regenerated from the pinned Java dependency.
- `cargo test --offline -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib acl_expand_ip_matches_ -- --nocapture` — passed; Turkish and Lithuanian child-process locale cases.
- `cargo test --workspace --locked` — passed.
- `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked` — passed.
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` — passed.
- `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` — passed; 37 differential scenarios, 36 route/VIP cases, 106 typed-header cross-decodes, and 19 typed-body cross-decodes.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — passed.

The first fixture-generation attempt used an ineffective `-Dexec.mainClass`
override and reached `compat.Main` usage output; the supported `acl-fixture`
command above regenerated it successfully. An initial run against the expanded
marks also caught the UTF-16 padding discrepancy before the correction.

## Scope and remaining evidence

This closes the Lithuanian uppercase context and UTF-16 segment-width slices
for the invoked direct helper inputs. It does not close broad P18-V01
reconciliation. Current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows runtime, and
Phase 19 Broker/Docker scenarios remain open. No external CI or Broker was
used. The four pre-existing protected Phase 19 worktree paths remain
unstaged and untouched.
